@@ -13,3 +13,9 @@ Each line of an events file is a JSON object:
 Collectors run in several regions and stamp events with their own UTC offset. Legacy collectors (anything installed before 2024) write naive timestamps such as `2024-03-09 22:10:00`; those are UTC. Blank lines are ignored.
 
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
+
+## Recent events only
+
+    python -m evlog report events.jsonl --since 2024-03-10
+
+counts only events at or after the given date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, or a full ISO 8601 timestamp). A date means midnight UTC; a value without a UTC offset is taken as UTC. Event offsets are taken into account, so an event stamped `2024-03-12T08:15:00+09:00` is compared as 2024-03-11 23:15 UTC.
